.TH BUFFER_STUBBORN_READ 3
.SH NAME
buffer_stubborn_read \- perform a read operation while ignoring interrupts

.SH SYNTAX
.B #include <lib/buffer.h>
.br
.B ssize_t buffer_stubborn_read(buffer_op_proto* op, fd_type fd, const void* buf, size_t len, void* ptr);

.SH DESCRIPTION
.B buffer_stubborn_read
performs a read (or read-like) operation on the file descriptor
.IR fd ,
storing the result in
.IR buf
of length
.IR len .
The actual operation is performed by calling the function pointer
.IR op ,
passing
.IR fd ,
.IR buf ,
.IR len ,
and the opaque pointer
.IR ptr .

Unlike a standard system read,
.B buffer_stubborn_read
automatically retries the operation if
.IR op
returns an error with
.I errno
set to
.BR EINTR .
This is useful for ensuring that signals do not prematurely abort I/O operations.

.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes read on success (the value returned by
.IR op ),
or -1 on error (with
.I errno
set appropriately by
.IR op ).

.SH SEE ALSO
buffer(3), read(2)